feat(spmi): add read-only PMIC arbiter access for the PON probe

The fastboot restart-reason experiment writes the Qualcomm cookie to IMEM,
but the next boot never sees it.  The vendor path also writes the PMIC PON
RESTART_REASON, and this kernel cannot even read the PMIC because there is
no SPMI controller driver.  Add the read-only half of one, in the style of
the UFS, USB and touch bring-up drivers: MMIO through ml_io_map, no IOKit,
no interrupts, bounded polling, console output only.

Three gates are exposed as console commands:

  SPMI?  SPMI-1: map the arbiter and read core+0x0; identify the version and
         stop unless it is a known family (only the v5 arithmetic is
         implemented).
         SPMI-2: walk core+0x900 + 4*apid, bounded by the DT "core" size,
         read the ownership register at cnfg+0x700 + 4*apid, print every
         non-zero mapping entry, and print the raw mapping/ownership
         registers for every APID that maps PPID 0x008 (PM8150 PON, SID 0).
         A PPID that cannot exist is walked first as a negative control.
  PON?   SPMI-3: select the APID owned by EE 0 (the first mapping if none is),
         then read PON subtype 0x0805 and SOFT_RB_SPARE 0x088F through the
         observer channel twice each and require the two reads to agree.

The v5 observer arithmetic is obsrvr + 0x10000*ee + 0x80*apid, not the
read/write chnls + 0x10000*apid; the difference is documented where it is
used.  Nothing writes a PMIC register: issuing an observer read writes the
arbiter's command register, which is the read request itself.  The masked
read-modify-write (SPMI-4) is deliberately not implemented.

Addresses are the kona.dtsi ones: core 0x0C440000+0x1100, obsrvr
0x0E600000+0x100000, cnfg 0x0C40A000+0x26000, qcom,ee = 0, qcom,channel = 0.
chnls and intr are not mapped because the kernel's io_map submap is 8 MiB in
total and the 32 MiB channel window is only needed by a write path.
